1
00:03:51,818 --> 00:03:57,818
She was a perfect doll. Now she's the real thing.

2
00:07:43,636 --> 00:07:49,636
Life-Size is a family, comedy, fantasy film directed by Mark Rosman.

3
00:11:35,454 --> 00:11:41,454
Sad and lonely after the death of her mother, Casey
would do anything to see her again.

4
00:15:27,272 --> 00:15:33,272
But when a series of mystic mishaps mistakenly brings her fashion doll
“Eve” to life instead, it changes Casey’s world forever!

5
00:19:19,090 --> 00:19:25,090
Casey Stuart, played by Lindsay Lohan.

6
00:23:10,909 --> 00:23:16,909
Eve, played by Tyra Banks.

7
00:27:02,727 --> 00:27:08,727
Ben Stuart, played by Jere Burns.

8
00:30:54,545 --> 00:31:00,545
Drew McDonald, played by Anne Marie DeLuise.

9
00:34:46,363 --> 00:34:52,363
Richie, played by Garwin Sanford.

10
00:38:38,181 --> 00:38:44,181
Phil, played by Tom Butler.

11
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Life-Size is a 2000 American fantasy comedy television film directed by
Mark Rosman and starring Lindsay Lohan and Tyra Banks.

12
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
It originally premiered on March 5, 2000, on ABC as part
of The Wonderful World of Disney block.

13
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:19,636
Lohan portrays a young girl who casts a magic spell to bring back her deceased mother and,
instead, accidentally brings to life her fashion doll, played by Banks.

14
00:54:05,454 --> 00:54:11,454
The film then follows their relationship as the doll creates
havoc while trying to fit into the real world.

15
00:57:57,272 --> 00:58:03,272
Life-Size was popular among its demographic, developing a cult following that frequently revisited and reexamined it
in the years following its release, and generated a sequel 18 years after the original broadcast.

16
01:01:49,090 --> 01:01:55,090
It is considered a didactic children's film that set the tone for doll-inspired movies and is perceived by many fans as "the first
live-action Barbie movie" due to the similarities between the two dolls despite not having the rights to the official character.

17
01:05:40,909 --> 01:05:46,909
The film made its streaming debut on Disney+ in November 2025, after
previously never having been available through digital platforms.

18
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
The sequel, titled Life-Size 2: A Christmas Eve, premiered on
December 2, 2018 on Freeform with Banks reprising her role.

19
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
In 2020, Banks announced another sequel was in the works.

20
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
The film explores themes of american football, sorcery,
single father, doll, death of mother.

21
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
The tone is lighthearted.
